# Shooter — Editor-Placed Targets + ShooterController

## Problem

Current `TargetSpawner.cs` spawns targets at runtime in random positions via object pooling. This doesn't allow blending targets into hand-crafted scenery. `Target.cs` reports score directly to `GameManager.Instance` with no central shooter-level controller.

`TargetController.cs` is a legacy duplicate of Target's fall logic — unused, no namespace.

## Proposed Architecture

```
ShooterController (singleton-ish per scene)
 ├── Manages score relay → GameManager
 ├── Manages spawn waves (activate/deactivate pre-placed targets)
 ├── Tracks active targets → detects game-end conditions
 └── Receives OnTargetKilled(Target) notifications

Target (on each pre-placed GameObject in scene)
 ├── Row ID (0=near, 1=mid, 2=far)  
 ├── TargetType (Bandit/Innocent)
 ├── OnHit() → notifies ShooterController
 ├── Fall animation → stays deactivated until next wave
 └── Registers/unregisters with ShooterController on Enable/Disable
```

```mermaid
sequenceDiagram
    participant Editor as Scene (Editor-placed targets)
    participant SC as ShooterController
    participant T as Target
    participant GM as GameManager
    participant HUD as HUDController

    Note over SC: StartRound() → activates wave of targets
    SC->>T: SetActive(true) for selected targets
    T->>SC: RegisterTarget(this) [OnEnable]
    Note over T: Player shoots...
    T->>SC: OnTargetKilled(this, type, row)
    SC->>GM: AddScore(points)
    SC->>SC: _activeCount--, check wave complete
    T->>T: Fall animation → SetActive(false)
    T->>SC: UnregisterTarget(this) [OnDisable]
    Note over SC: All targets killed → next wave or end game
```

